---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Product | Open Replicant">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero__content">
      <span class="badge badge--open-source">Open source · Apache-2.0</span>
      <h1>Product</h1>
      <p class="hero__tagline">
        Morphogen is self-managing AI infrastructure. A system you describe —
        which builds and manages itself, starting with itself.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card__accent" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h3>Knowledge kernel</h3>
        <p>
          A governed record where model output is only ever a proposal. Every
          claim is attributed (agent and run) and referenced; extracted claims
          carry the supporting quote. Nothing is deleted — claims are
          superseded, refuted, or retracted by status.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card__accent" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h3>MAPE-K loop</h3>
        <p>
          Monitor telemetry → analyse anomalies → plan with a prediction →
          human review → act → verify the prediction held. Every step is a
          swappable slot with a defined contract. Extensions act before the
          commit (validate, veto, route) or after it (follow the change feed).
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card__accent" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h3>Self-modifying (G2)</h3>
        <p>
          Morphogen proposes a change to one of its own providers, builds it,
          installs it in a sandbox, scores it against the incumbent, and waits
          for your approval. Only when the observed result matches the
          prediction does it commit.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>What it manages</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card__accent" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h3>Systems it didn't build (G3)</h3>
        <p>
          Morphogen maps a real system it did not build — like podinfo with
          Redis — from its compose file, watches it, and completes one governed
          change on it. Every step cites the one before.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card__accent" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h3>Described, not hand-built</h3>
        <p>
          An interview becomes a system map. Gaps become questions. A complete
          map becomes a deployable compose file you approve before anything
          runs.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card__accent" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h3>Review lane</h3>
        <p>
          Autonomy level × risk class decides what needs a person's sign-in.
          Plans show their citations, belief, prediction, and risk. Approved or
          refused — by a person, as themselves.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a href="https://github.com/openreplicant/morphogen" class="btn btn--large btn--outline">View on GitHub</a>
      <a href="/contribute/" class="btn btn--large">Contribute to the project</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
